From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:01:30 +0900
Subject: Cast: keep the TV running with the app in the background or the
 screen off

With the phone surface suspended, render_all now serves only the cast
window: its new buffers go to the TV presenter and only it gets frame
callbacks. The compositor loop waits on the Wayland fds instead of the
phone's Choreographer, so the TV keeps KWin's own 60 Hz pace even with
the phone screen off.

Cast presentation feedback is reported on the cast output at its own
refresh rate (the phone's rate kept switching CAST-1 between 120 and
30 Hz) and for every cast commit. An unchanged TV buffer is no longer
presented again on every phone frame. update_output_mode skips windows
when nothing changed, and native-stats gains cast counters.

KWin moto14: a host configure without a size change no longer
re-queries the outputs. Returning to the foreground rebuilt every
output's scene view and could leave the cast output frozen for good.
APK 1.33.

Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-26
X-Rungic-Status: Inappropriate [Android host specific: runs nested in the Android APK compositor]
X-Rungic-Tests: none (gap: casting needs a TV receiver; manual list)
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/58
Origin: vendor, commit:5c6e0958
---
 src/backends/wayland/wayland_output.cpp | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/backends/wayland/wayland_output.cpp b/src/backends/wayland/wayland_output.cpp
index 212d20a..05e8a13 100644
--- a/src/backends/wayland/wayland_output.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/wayland/wayland_output.cpp
@@ -553,7 +553,17 @@ void WaylandOutput::applyConfigure(const QSize &size, quint32 serial)
     m_xdgShellSurface->ackConfigure(serial);
     if (!size.isEmpty()) {
         const bool androidOutput = qEnvironmentVariableIsSet("MOTO_KWIN_FLAT_OUTPUT");
-        auto mode = std::make_shared<OutputMode>(androidOutput ? size : size * m_pendingScale, m_refreshRate);
+        const QSize pixels = androidOutput ? size : size * m_pendingScale;
+        // Moto (docs/58): the host configures its windows again without a size
+        // change, e.g. when the Android app returns to the foreground. That is not
+        // an output change; re-querying the outputs rebuilt every output's scene
+        // view, and a burst of these left the cast output's clients without frame
+        // callbacks, freezing the TV.
+        if (m_state.currentMode && m_state.currentMode->size() == pixels && m_state.currentMode->refreshRate() == m_refreshRate
+            && m_state.scale == (androidOutput ? m_state.scale : m_pendingScale)) {
+            return;
+        }
+        auto mode = std::make_shared<OutputMode>(pixels, m_refreshRate);
 
         State next = m_state;
         next.modes = androidPrimary() ? androidModes(size, m_refreshRate) : QList{mode};
